+// its author's own code), the runtime, and the shared prelude and anchor beside the entry. Anything else (an app's
+// worker.js, a `data:` module, an import of either) may not name the compiler's intrinsics (refuse.js).
+// The two names are compared as real paths: a temp dir under a symlink (/var on macOS) reaches the loader as both spellings.
+const realPath = p => { try { return fs.realpathSync(p); } catch { return p; } };
